# apps/mobile env template — copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined into the JS bundle at build/export time
# (Expo auto-loads .env / .env.local from this app's root).
#
# These are NOT committed: eas.json build profiles carry no env block, so the
# backend hosts are never tracked. Local builds read .env.local (below). EAS
# cloud builds read EAS-hosted env, set PER ENVIRONMENT — `--profile preview`
# resolves to the `preview` env (staging host), `--profile production` to the
# `production` env (prod host); a var set in one is NOT seen by the other.
# See docs/dev/deployment.md "Mobile app build-time env".

# Backend the app talks to. Simulator defaults to http://localhost:3000;
# a physical device needs the Mac's LAN IP.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.42:3000

# Public web origin for shareable links (the /join/<code> invite URL).
# In prod set this to the real domain. If unset, falls back to the API URL
# above so local-deployment links resolve against the same backend.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_WEB_URL=https://verre.app
